From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:07:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 75/78] PlaitOS: plait_backup system service

Plait Backup (the app with Android-DataBackup's UI) gets root-depth app
backups on a locked PlaitOS through this Binder service: installd
streams the data (its new plait* calls), this service decides who may.

Every call carries a grant the Plait Broker manager signed (same token
as the broker's GrantToken). It counts only if the signature checks
out against the manager's key, the manager is app.plait.broker as it
came in the system image (never updated), the caller is the uid,
package and signing certificate the grant names (own user only), the
grant covers the scope and target and has not expired, and the manager
still reports it active. Uses go to the manager's audit log.

- backupPart / restorePart: CE, DE, Android/data, obb, media as
  tar.zst (Android-DataBackup's layout); restores force-stop the app.
- backupApks / installApks: base + split APKs; installs go through a
  PackageInstaller session pinned to the package name.
- getState / restoreState: granted runtime permissions and app-ops.
  Restores only grant runtime permissions the app requests, and only
  loosen app-ops whose permission the app requests.
- Never a target: the broker, the backup app, android, shared system
  uids.

